<title>SINGAPORE: India awards July 6-8 Madras LAN at minus $21/T.</title>
<headline>India awards July 6-8 Madras LAN at minus $21/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>India has awarded its tender to sell 27,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting from Madras July 6-8 at $21 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board basis, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The tender offering the cargo from the east coast closed June 25 and was valid until June 26.</p>
<p>IOC's last Madras LAN cargo, lifted in June, was awarded at $22 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes fob to a South Korean refiner, sources said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
